s not create capacity. If jobs arrive faster than they finish for long enough, the oldest job gets older until the promised completion time is missed."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-0",{"id":"calculate-the-backlog-before-scaling","children":"Calculate the backlog before scaling"}],"\n",["$","p","p-1",{"children":["Suppose export requests arrive at ",["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"120 jobs/minute"}]," during a 20-minute peak. Six workers each complete ","$L19",", so service capacity is ","$L1a",". Backlog grows at ","$L1b",", reaching about ","$L1c"," after 20 minutes. Once arrivals return to ","$L1d",", spare capacity is ","$L1e"," and draining those 600 jobs takes another ","$L1f",". A 20-minute burst can therefore affect users for roughly 40 minutes."]}],"\n","$L20","\n","$L21","\n","$L22","\n","$L23","\n","$L24","\n","$L25","\n","$L26","\n","$L27","\n","$L28","\n","$L29","\n","$L2a","\n","$L2b","\n","$L2c","\n","$L2d","\n","$L2e","\n","$L2f","\n","$L30","\n","$L31"],false]}]]}],"$L32"]}]}]
