2a:["$","p","p-7",{"children":"Scale on a signal close to user impact, such as oldest job age relative to a completion target, while considering queue depth and worker utilization. Queue depth alone has no universal “bad” value: 600 one-second jobs and 600 ten-minute jobs are different. If the dependency is the bottleneck, more workers amplify failure. Apply backpressure at intake or worker concurrency instead."}]
